You are the third of three testing angles on SFCC-11 Cart epic build plan step 4.6 (`overrides/app/pages/cart/cartDrawerContainer.tsx`, new; `overrides/app/pages/cart/cartDrawerContainer.test.tsx`, new; `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmCartDrawer/index.tsx` + `index.test.tsx`, modified). Branch `feature/SFCC-11_cart`, already checked out — do not switch branches, do not commit, do not push, do not stage anything.

YOUR LANE: you have EXCLUSIVE, sole rights to mutate the filesystem for this task right now — two sibling agents already finished their pure-read investigation (ticket/AC/SDK-typing, and structure/imports/a11y/DRY) before you started, so there is no concurrent reader to corrupt. You own all mutation-testing and live-render probes. Do ONE change at a time, run the narrowly-scoped test command, capture the real output, then IMMEDIATELY revert before starting the next — confirm via `git diff <file>` that each file is back to byte-identical original before moving to the next mutation. At the very end, run `git status --porcelain` and `git diff --stat` and confirm the ONLY changes present are the pre-existing ones already on this branch (modified: `zimmCartDrawer/index.tsx`, `zimmCartDrawer/index.test.tsx`; untracked: `cartDrawerContainer.tsx`, `cartDrawerContainer.test.tsx`) — nothing else, no leftover temp files. This is the highest-risk step in the whole plan; do not leave the tree dirty.

Read `overrides/app/pages/cart/cartDrawerContainer.tsx` (431 lines) and `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmCartDrawer/index.tsx` in full yourself before starting.

REQUIRED WORK, IN PRIORITY ORDER (do all of these; the bonus items after are only if time/budget remains):

**1. Mutation test — Fix 1 (ZimmCartDrawer renders children unconditionally).**
File: `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmCartDrawer/index.tsx`, line ~83: `<chakra.div __css={styles.body}>{children}</chakra.div>`.
Mutate to recreate the OLD behaviour the code comment (lines 79-82) and `~/Dev/zimmerMANN-skills/.runs/SFCC-11/plan.md` line 522 describe: `<chakra.div __css={styles.body}>{itemCount === 0 ? <chakra.p>Your bag is empty.</chakra.p> : children}</chakra.div>`.
Run: `npx vitest run overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmCartDrawer/index.test.tsx`.
Expected: RED, specifically the "renders children even when itemCount is 0 — no hardcoded placeholder takes its place" test. Paste the real failure output. Then revert and confirm clean.

**2. Mutation test — pass criterion 2 (render guard runs from an effect, not the render body).**
File: `overrides/app/pages/cart/cartDrawerContainer.tsx`, lines ~233-240:
```
useEffect(() => {
    if (!basket?.basketId) return;
    void capBasketQuantities(basket).then((result) => {
      if (result.status === 'corrected') {
        notifyMaxQuantityReached();
      }
    });
  }, [basket]);
```
Mutate by deleting the `useEffect` wrapper and running the same guarded call directly in the render body at the same location (still inside the component function, just not inside `useEffect(...)`).
Run: `npx vitest run overrides/app/pages/cart/cartDrawerContainer.test.tsx`.
Expected: RED, specifically "does not re-call capBasketQuantities on a second render that leaves the basket unchanged (proves the effect dependency, not the render body, drives it)" — that test's own comment (lines 341-352 of the test file) documents exactly this mutation as the thing it exists to catch. Paste the real output. Then revert and confirm clean.

**3. Mutation test — Fix 3 (wishlist-resume waits for merge-then-cap to settle).**
File: `overrides/app/pages/cart/cartDrawerContainer.tsx`, lines ~285-297:
```
useEffect(() => {
    if (!isRegistered) {
      setIsGuestState(true);
      return;
    }
    if (!hasPendingPostAuthSettleRef.current || queryClient.isMutating() === 0) {
      hasPendingPostAuthSettleRef.current = false;
      setIsGuestState(false);
    }
  }, [isRegistered, isMutatingSignal, queryClient]);
```
Mutate by deleting the wait condition so it always flips once registered:
```
useEffect(() => {
    if (!isRegistered) {
      setIsGuestState(true);
      return;
    }
    setIsGuestState(false);
  }, [isRegistered, isMutatingSignal, queryClient]);
```
Run: `npx vitest run overrides/app/pages/cart/cartDrawerContainer.test.tsx`.
Expected: RED, specifically "isGuest stays true after auth-success while mutations are in flight, and flips to false only once they drain". Paste the real output. Then revert and confirm clean.

**4. Live-render falsification — does `ProductItem` actually render correctly with the merged product shape?**
The existing `cartDrawerContainer.test.tsx` fully mocks `app/components/product-item` (see its lines ~129-133), so nothing today proves the REAL `ProductItem` renders correctly with the exact merged object the container builds (`{...basketLineItem, ...fetchedProduct, price: basketLineItem.price, quantity: basketLineItem.quantity, isProductUnavailable}` — see cartDrawerContainer.tsx lines 391-408). Create a NEW temporary test file (pick an unused name like `overrides/app/pages/cart/__tester_probe_productitem.test.tsx`) that imports the REAL default export of `app/components/product-item`, builds a merged object the same way the container does (use realistic field shapes — not just empty arrays for `imageGroups`/`variationAttributes`/`variationValues`; check `overrides/app/components/product-item/index.test.tsx` and/or `index.stories.test.tsx` for what realistic fixtures and required providers/mocks look like, e.g. `ZimmIcon` mock per testing.md's documented Vitest gap, `ChakraProvider`, possibly `MultiSiteProvider`/`IntlProvider`), and renders `<ProductItem product={merged} secondaryActions={<div>test</div>} />`. Assert it renders without throwing, and that it displays the expected name/price/image-derived content — not just "didn't crash." Capture any console errors/warnings. Then DELETE the temp file and confirm `git status` shows no trace of it.

**5. Live-render falsification — does `CartWishlistAuthGate`'s composition actually work?**
It's not exported, so it can only be exercised through `CartDrawerContainer` itself. The existing test suite mocks `ZimmAuthDrawerContent`/`AuthModal`/`OtpAuth` and never sets the mocked `wishlistAuthDrawer.isOpen` to `true`, so the real open → real content → real close behaviour is never exercised. Create a NEW temporary test file that renders the full container (mirror `cartDrawerContainer.test.tsx`'s own mock setup for `useCurrentBasket`/`useProducts`/etc.) but this time does NOT mock `app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmAuthDrawerContent` — use the real one (check `zimmAuthDrawerContent/index.test.tsx` for what it needs to render without crashing, e.g. its child `SocialButtons` imports icons directly per the existing container test's own comment at lines 94-100). Set the mocked `useWishlistAuthDrawer` to return `isOpen: true`, `isPasswordlessEnabled: true`, and working `emailValue`/`onEmailChange`/`onSendCode` stubs. Assert: (a) a second dialog/drawer with real auth content actually appears (e.g. a real email textbox rendered by the real `ZimmAuthDrawerContent`, not a stub), (b) closing it (call the mocked `handleDrawerClose` and re-render with `isOpen: false`, or simulate Escape if the real close path is reachable) actually removes that content. While you have this real render up, ALSO check: a sibling read-only agent traced `zimmDrawer/index.tsx`'s `handleCloseComplete` (lines ~292-294: `if (finalFocusRef) finalFocusRef.current?.focus();`) and found `finalFocusRef` is never passed to Chakra's actual `<Drawer>` — meaning Chakra's own internal FocusLock/`ModalFocusScope` might still apply some OTHER native focus-restore behaviour independent of that manual mechanism. With your real render, close the wishlist auth drawer and check what element actually ends up focused (`document.activeElement`) — does it match the manual-mechanism prediction (effectively nothing/body), or does Chakra's FocusLock do something else on its own? This directly answers a question the sibling agent explicitly left open for you. Then delete the temp file and confirm clean.

**BONUS (only if the required 5 above are fully done and clean, and budget remains):**

6. A React-logic-correctness fixture for the "prop seeds state on mount" edge case: `const [isGuestState, setIsGuestState] = useState(!isRegistered)` (line 271) only seeds once at mount. Write one temporary test rendering the container with `isRegistered: true` at mount (so `isGuestState` seeds to `false`), then re-render with `isRegistered: false` on a later render (simulating a session invalidation) via the mocked `useCustomerType`, and confirm `isGuestState`/`data-is-guest` correctly flips back to `true` reactively rather than staying stuck at the stale mount-time seed (the gating `useEffect`'s own `if (!isRegistered) { setIsGuestState(true); return; }` branch at lines 286-289 should handle this — confirm it actually does). Delete the temp file after.

7. Quick check (not a full investigation): does `overrides/app/components/product-item/index.tsx` actually have a `showLoading` prop with the shape the container's own docblock (lines 52-54) implies it could use for a future "isRemoving" feature? Just grep/read, no test needed.

REPORT FORMAT: for each of the 5 required items (and any bonus items attempted), state the real command you ran, the real output (paste actual failure/pass text, not a paraphrase), and CONFIRMED/PLAUSIBLE + 🔴/🟡/🔵 + UNIFORM/ONE-OFF for any defect found. End with explicit confirmation that `git status --porcelain` is back to exactly the pre-existing diff with nothing extra, and a one-line note on anything you could not complete and why.

